    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>Weapon (Greatsword), Artifact (Requires Attunement)</em></p><p>When dragon magic split King Varian Wrynn into two versions of himself, one of his selves wielded the night elven blade <em>Shalla’tor</em>, while the other wielded the night elven blade <em>Ellemayne</em>. Varian eventually merged his twin selves back into one whole. In doing so, he inadvertently fused the blades into a new weapon called <em>Shalamayne</em>.</p><p>The Jailer, one of the rulers of the Shadowlands, once stole and reforged <em>Shalamayne</em> into a mourneblade called Kingsmourne. But Varian’s son, Anduin Wrynn, later restored <em>Shalamayne</em> to its rightful form. Anduin is the sword’s last known wielder.</p><p><strong>Magic Weapon.</strong> You gain a +3 bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls made with this magic weapon. It deals an extra 2d12 Force damage on a hit.</p><p><strong>Dual Mastery.</strong> If you have the Weapon Mastery feature and choose Greatsword as one of your mastered weapons, you can use both the Graze and Sap mastery properties at once while wielding <em>Shalamayne</em>.</p><p><strong>Splitting and Reuniting the Sword.</strong> While holding <em>Shalamayne</em>, you can take a Magic action to end your Attunement to the weapon and split it into two magic swords: <em>Shalla’tor</em> and <em>Ellemayne</em>. Each is a +3 Longsword with the Finesse and Light properties. A creature who holds both swords can take a Magic action to rejoin them into <em>Shalamayne</em>, attuning to the weapon instantly.</p><p><strong>Random Properties.</strong> <em>Shalamayne</em> has the following random properties:</p><ul><li><p>2 minor beneficial properties</p></li><li><p>1 major beneficial property</p></li></ul><p><strong>Destroying Shalamayne.</strong> One can destroy <em>Shalamayne</em> by splitting it into <em>Shalla’tor</em> and <em>Ellemayne</em>, then burying one or both swords at the roots of a World Tree in the Emerald Dream. After one year, the buried swords dissolve into the soil.</p><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-gJZWVbN55t0uoFDL\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p>Pour séparer l’épée, remplacez-la par deux Longswords +3 avec Finesse et Light, par exemple avec le modèle <em>Weapon, +1, +2, or +3</em> de dnd5e. <em>Dual Mastery</em> est à appliquer à la main. Les propriétés aléatoires d’artefact sont à ajouter par le MJ.</p></section>",
